IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa17-helpers`
IMPORT `coa17-part21-ch1`
IMPORT `coa17-regulative`

-- coa17-tests-regulative.l4: #TRACE runs of the regulative rules of coa17-regulative.l4. check.sh counts assertion lines only,
-- and a DEONTIC value cannot be compared in #ASSERT on the stable binary, so the outcome of each trace is printed, not counted:
-- coa17-check-traces.sh runs this file with both builds and compares the printed outcomes with the list written below, one per
-- trace, in order. The expected outcome is decided from the text of the section named beside each trace: an act on the last day is
-- in time (FULFILLED); an act on the day after is not (BREACH). Day 0 of every trace is the day the period begins.

§ `Traces: the regulative rules`

`s 769(1) test allotment of shares on 5 January 2026` MEANS `s 769 allotment` WITH
    `s 769(1) the thing allotted` IS `s 769(1) shares allotted`
    `s 769(1) the day of the allotment` IS Date 5 1 2026
    `s 769(2)(a) the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS FALSE
    `s 769(2)(b) the allotment is to a financial institution` IS FALSE
    `s 769(2)(c) the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares allotted` IS FALSE

`s 769(1) test allotment to a financial institution` MEANS `s 769 allotment` WITH
    `s 769(1) the thing allotted` IS `s 769(1) shares allotted`
    `s 769(1) the day of the allotment` IS Date 5 1 2026
    `s 769(2)(a) the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS FALSE
    `s 769(2)(b) the allotment is to a financial institution` IS TRUE
    `s 769(2)(c) the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares allotted` IS FALSE

`s 771(1) test transfer lodged on 5 January 2026` MEANS `s 771 lodged transfer` WITH
    `s 771(1) the day the transfer was lodged` IS Date 5 1 2026
    `s 771(5)(a) the transfer is of shares and the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares` IS FALSE
    `s 771(5)(b) the transfer is a transmission of shares or debentures by operation of law` IS FALSE

`s 776(1) test transfer lodged on 5 January 2026` MEANS `s 776 lodged transfer` WITH
    `s 776(1) the thing transferred` IS `s 776(1) shares transferred`
    `s 776(1) the day the transfer was lodged` IS Date 5 1 2026
    `s 776(2)(a) the transfer is duly stamped and otherwise valid` IS TRUE
    `s 776(2)(b) the transfer is an exempt transfer within the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS FALSE
    `s 776(2) the company is entitled to refuse to register the transfer and does not register it` IS FALSE
    `s 776(3)(a) the conditions of issue provide otherwise` IS FALSE
    `s 776(3)(b) the transfer is to a financial institution` IS FALSE
    `s 776(3)(c) the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares transferred` IS FALSE
    `s 777(1) the transferee is not entitled to a certificate by virtue of regulations under section 3 of the Stock Transfer Act 1982` IS FALSE
    `s 777(2)(a) the transferee has since become entitled to a certificate by virtue of a provision of those regulations` IS FALSE
    `s 777(2)(b) the day on which the transferee gave the company notice in writing of that fact` IS NOTHING

-- s 769(1): allotted 5 January, ready on day 59 = 5 March, the last day.
#TRACE `s 769(1) the company's duty to have the documents ready (regulative rule)` `s 769(1) test allotment of shares on 5 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 769(1) complete and have ready for delivery the documents` AT 59
-- s 769(1): ready on day 60 = 6 March, one day late.
#TRACE `s 769(1) the company's duty to have the documents ready (regulative rule)` `s 769(1) test allotment of shares on 5 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 769(1) complete and have ready for delivery the documents` AT 60
-- s 769(2)(b): allotment to a financial institution, no duty: a late act changes nothing.
#TRACE `s 769(1) the company's duty to have the documents ready (regulative rule)` `s 769(1) test allotment to a financial institution` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 769(1) complete and have ready for delivery the documents` AT 60
-- s 771(1)(a): registered on day 59 = 5 March.
#TRACE `s 771(1) the company's duty to register the transfer or give notice of refusal (regulative rule)` `s 771(1) test transfer lodged on 5 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 771(1)(a) register the transfer` AT 59
-- s 771(1)(b): notice of refusal with reasons on day 59.
#TRACE `s 771(1) the company's duty to register the transfer or give notice of refusal (regulative rule)` `s 771(1) test transfer lodged on 5 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 771(1)(b) give the transferee notice of refusal with its reasons` AT 59
-- s 771(1)(a): registered on day 60, one day late.
#TRACE `s 771(1) the company's duty to register the transfer or give notice of refusal (regulative rule)` `s 771(1) test transfer lodged on 5 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 771(1)(a) register the transfer` AT 60
-- s 776(1): lodged 5 January, ready on 5 March.
#TRACE `s 776(1) the company's duty to have the documents ready after a transfer (regulative rule)` `s 776(1) test transfer lodged on 5 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 776(1) complete and have ready for delivery the documents after a transfer` AT 59
-- s 776(1): ready one day late.
#TRACE `s 776(1) the company's duty to have the documents ready after a transfer (regulative rule)` `s 776(1) test transfer lodged on 5 January 2026` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `s 776(1) complete and have ready for delivery the documents after a transfer` AT 60
